owth is nothing short of incredible.\nMicron reports Q4 results on Sept. 30, and the average Wall Street analyst expects 348% revenue growth year over year. For fiscal year 2027 (ending August 2027), analysts expect an additional 85% growth. Those are some incredible growth rates, and could be low projections if the memory chip shortage worsens.\nMicron's management team believes the market will be supply-constrained beyond 2027, leaving plenty of time for Micron to benefit from soaring memory chip prices, and investors should reap the benefits of this growth over the next few years.\n3. Nebius Group\nNebius may be a bit more under the radar than the other two, but it's also the fastest-growing of the three. It's a neocloud computing business, which means it provides cloud computing services dedicated to AI. This is obviously a hot industry to be in right now, and Nebius' growth results showcase it.\nDuring Q2, its revenue skyrocketed 454% year over year. That was primarily due to more computing capacity coming online, as it has rapidly increased its contracted computing power. In August last year, it had around 1 gigawatt of power contracts. This year, that figure has risen to 5 gigawatts.\nNebius is building and renting data centers as quickly as it can get its hands on them, as there is more than enough demand to drive these activities. But Q2's growth wasn't the peak either.\nFor 2026, the analyst community expects 533% revenue growth. For 2027, it expects 257% growth. That easily places Nebius on top of the list of fastest-growing stocks, and with the stock price down around 30% from its all-time high, now could be the perfect buying opportunity.\nBy Keithen Drury – Sep 5, 2026 at 9:44AM EST"
